1
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:03,130
[CHALLE]
I won't let you go.

2
00:00:04,290 --> 00:00:06,290
Huh! What happened?

3
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:08,500
[door opens]

4
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:15,540
Huh?

5
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:20,250
[ORLAND]
It's you.

6
00:00:20,330 --> 00:00:21,330
[chuckles]

7
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:22,670
[whooshes]

8
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:27,500
[CHALLE]
No one will take you.

9
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:30,130
I gave you my word.

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,330
I'll protect you.

11
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:35,210
[ANNE gasps]

12
00:00:35,290 --> 00:00:37,170
[ORLAND screams]

13
00:00:37,250 --> 00:00:39,000
- [groans]
- [ELLIOTT] Orland!

14
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,750
[panting]

15
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:42,210
[KING]
Are you all right!?

16
00:00:42,290 --> 00:00:44,130
[gasps]

17
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:46,880
- [gasps]
- [NADIR] There's so, much blood.

18
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:48,330
- [KING] Let's take him inside!
- [VALENTINE] This is bad.

19
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:49,880
[ELLIOTT]
Wait! Be careful!

20
00:02:22,210 --> 00:02:23,420
[ELLIOTT]
Daana, Hal!

21
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:25,540
- Go boil some water now!
- [DAANA] Yes!

22
00:02:25,630 --> 00:02:28,630
- Bandages, too!
- [ORLAND] My eye. He got my eye.

23
00:02:28,710 --> 00:02:29,960
[groans]

24
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:31,710
So, someone attacked you?

25
00:02:31,790 --> 00:02:35,080
[ORLAND] Yes. The one
we met on the highway.

26
00:02:35,170 --> 00:02:36,290
The red fairy.

27
00:02:36,380 --> 00:02:38,920
[ELLIOTT]
Oh! I thought that was over.

28
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,210
He came back for us?

29
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:41,830
♪

30
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:43,540
[CHALLE]
He's been here all along.

31
00:02:43,630 --> 00:02:45,210
[ALL sigh]

32
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:47,630
He introduced himself as Gladus.

33
00:02:47,710 --> 00:02:50,080
We were fooled.
I should've been more careful.

34
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:55,040
[panting] If he's Gladus,
then what about Bridget?

35
00:02:55,130 --> 00:02:57,630
[gasps]

36
00:02:58,630 --> 00:03:00,080
It can't be.

37
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:04,330
[sobs]

38
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:05,420
Miss Bridget!

39
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:07,670
Hold on. I should go with you.

40
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:09,250
Thank you.

41
00:03:09,330 --> 00:03:11,380
Right, then.
I'll fetch a doctor.

42
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:12,540
And I'll go as well!

43
00:03:12,630 --> 00:03:14,170
You all mean
to abandon your work?

44
00:03:14,250 --> 00:03:15,580
[ALL sigh]

45
00:03:15,670 --> 00:03:17,250
[HUGH]
I'll arrange for the doctor.

46
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:18,880
I was about to leave anyway.

47
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:21,290
You don't mind helping us out?

48
00:03:23,170 --> 00:03:25,250
[HUGH]
I gave you Kat, didn't I?

49
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:26,420
If you don't finish in time

50
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:28,080
for the Holy
Beginnings Festival,

51
00:03:28,170 --> 00:03:30,460
that will leave me
in a very poor position.

52
00:03:31,710 --> 00:03:35,000
Besides, it's not just the Paige
Workshop's problem,

53
00:03:36,130 --> 00:03:37,920
I'll report it
to the Earl of Downing.

54
00:03:38,630 --> 00:03:40,920
"The red fairy who attacks
silver sugar masters

55
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,210
has reappeared."

56
00:03:43,210 --> 00:03:46,250
I will recommend that
he deploy soldiers for a search.

57
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:50,130
Lafalle fenn Lafalle, you said?

58
00:03:51,130 --> 00:03:52,830
The red fairy's true name.

59
00:03:53,790 --> 00:03:56,040
It sounds a bit like yours,
doesn't it?

60
00:03:56,790 --> 00:03:59,290
He said we were born
at the same place.

61
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:03,000
He wanted to make me his ally
but I refused him.

62
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:04,630
[ANNE]
What sort of "ally"?

63
00:04:04,710 --> 00:04:06,790
[CHALLE]
I don't know. But he said.

64
00:04:08,210 --> 00:04:09,380
[LAFALLE]
To even the odds of it,

65
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:11,170
I will be taking the girl.

66
00:04:11,250 --> 00:04:15,080
So you'll belong to me as well.
Yes, she is going to be mine.

67
00:04:15,790 --> 00:04:18,500
That doesn't make sense.
If he wants me,

68
00:04:18,580 --> 00:04:20,170
then why did he attack Orland?

69
00:04:20,250 --> 00:04:21,540
It's a warning.

70
00:04:21,630 --> 00:04:22,830
What he means is,

71
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:25,040
that he can attack you
any time he wants.

72
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:27,250
We're at his mercy.

73
00:04:27,330 --> 00:04:28,920
♪

74
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,380
[sobs]

75
00:04:37,130 --> 00:04:38,710
[CHALLE]
Don't leave my side.

76
00:04:38,790 --> 00:04:41,960
I will protect you
no matter what.

77
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:45,920
♪

78
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,330
[knocks]

79
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:48,710
[ANNE]
Miss Bridget?

80
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:52,830
[BRIDGET]
I'm the one who put Orland

81
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:54,420
through all of that, aren't I?

82
00:04:55,630 --> 00:04:57,630
I'm the one who brought Gladus.

83
00:04:57,710 --> 00:04:59,790
I'm the one
who brought that fairy here.

84
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:00,960
[gasps]

85
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,830
You can't blame this
on yourself!

86
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:05,000
The red fairy fooled
every last one of us!

87
00:05:05,080 --> 00:05:07,460
That includes me and Challe,
you know!

88
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:13,540
[BRIDGET] You don't have to lie.
It's my fault. I know that.

89
00:05:13,630 --> 00:05:15,500
[ANNE] No one is holding
this against you!

90
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:18,080
Stop it! I don't need your pity!

91
00:05:19,580 --> 00:05:20,670
Hmm!

92
00:05:20,750 --> 00:05:22,500
♪

93
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:25,500
A while ago there was
something Orland said.

94
00:05:26,210 --> 00:05:27,420
[ORLAND]
When we were young children,

95
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:28,380
we would play together.

96
00:05:29,290 --> 00:05:32,330
As a child,
she was cheerful and sweet but...

97
00:05:33,210 --> 00:05:34,080
[door opens]

98
00:05:34,170 --> 00:05:35,880
[BRIDGET]
You don't know a thing about me!

99
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:38,170
I'm not even allowed to
blame myself?

100
00:05:38,250 --> 00:05:39,580
So, what then?

101
00:05:39,670 --> 00:05:42,040
What do you propose
I do about this mess?

102
00:05:42,130 --> 00:05:45,630
♪

103
00:05:45,710 --> 00:05:46,830
[ANNE]
I don't know yet.

104
00:05:48,630 --> 00:05:51,380
We just need time to think.

105
00:05:52,750 --> 00:05:54,830
I'm sure there's something
that each of us can do

106
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:56,460
to get through this.

107
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:58,290
Let's figure that out first.

108
00:05:59,290 --> 00:06:00,920
[sniffs]

109
00:06:03,330 --> 00:06:05,290
[ELLIOTT]
I have some bad news.

110
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:08,290
I'm afraid Orland may
lose sight in his left eye.

111
00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:09,630
- [ALL gasp]
- That's awful!

112
00:06:10,830 --> 00:06:12,960
[ELLIOTT] And that isn't all
we have to worry about.

113
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:16,000
The fairy attacked him first
but Anne's next.

114
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,080
Huh!

115
00:06:17,170 --> 00:06:18,670
[ELLIOTT] If he appears again
and kidnaps her,

116
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:19,580
we can't continue.

117
00:06:20,330 --> 00:06:21,540
And if another one of us
is injured,

118
00:06:21,630 --> 00:06:23,630
it will slow down
the process too much.

119
00:06:24,250 --> 00:06:26,330
Even if Kat comes to help us,
we won't be able to finish

120
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:27,830
the work in time.

121
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:29,420
We'll have to forfeit the job.

122
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:33,420
Right now, we can still ask
the Silver Sugar Viscount

123
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:35,880
to lend us the extra sugar
that we need.

124
00:06:35,960 --> 00:06:38,420
It will put us at a disadvantage
for next year's selection,

125
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:41,250
and it may harm our
workshop's reputation a bit,

126
00:06:41,330 --> 00:06:43,580
but at least
we could finish the job.

127
00:06:43,670 --> 00:06:44,790
[ALL]
Hmm!

128
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:47,830
[ANNE]
We'll do it ourselves.

129
00:06:49,750 --> 00:06:51,170
We will find a way.

130
00:06:51,250 --> 00:06:52,880
♪

131
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:54,130
I believe in us.

132
00:06:56,250 --> 00:06:58,880
[NADIR]
I agree! Well said!

133
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:02,500
Right! If the Head of Artisans
says we'll succeed.

134
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:05,080
Then there's no point
in questioning ourselves!

135
00:07:05,170 --> 00:07:07,130
[ANNE]
Thank you! Let's work hard!

136
00:07:07,210 --> 00:07:08,540
- [NADIR] Always!
- [KING] We'll get it done.

137
00:07:08,630 --> 00:07:10,000
[VALENTINE]
Of course!

138
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:12,540
All right!
Back to work in a hurry!

139
00:07:12,630 --> 00:07:14,380
[chuckles]
- Yes, Sir. - Let's grind up...

140
00:07:14,460 --> 00:07:17,630
Mithril Lid Pod? Would
you mind helping us too?

141
00:07:17,710 --> 00:07:19,790
Any time! My pleasure!

142
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:21,380
[BOTH laugh]

143
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:25,630
♪

144
00:07:36,790 --> 00:07:38,630
[ANNE] I would be lying
if I said I wasn't afraid.

145
00:07:39,380 --> 00:07:41,920
Lafalle could come back here
at any time.

146
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,750
He could attack in an instant.

147
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:47,170
But I know that Challe
is here to protect me.

148
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:50,960
So, I'll concentrate
on the things I can control,

149
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:52,750
the things I can accomplish.

150
00:07:58,250 --> 00:08:00,330
Anne! The sun is up!

151
00:08:00,420 --> 00:08:02,210
- It's a brand-new day!
- Huh? Oh no! What happened!?

152
00:08:02,290 --> 00:08:03,580
[NOAH]
Come on, sleepyhead!

153
00:08:03,670 --> 00:08:05,540
[ANNE]
Huh! It's cold!

154
00:08:05,630 --> 00:08:08,380
- Noah? What's wrong?
- Why, nothing, Anne!

155
00:08:09,210 --> 00:08:10,750
I'm just doing my job!

156
00:08:10,830 --> 00:08:13,170
I've decided I want to help out
Daana and Hal.

157
00:08:13,250 --> 00:08:15,210
There's more than enough
work to do!

158
00:08:15,290 --> 00:08:18,460
And my first duty is to make
sure everyone's awake on time!

159
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:20,830
Hmm! Fine with me!

160
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:22,420
I'm just glad
you're cheering up!

161
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:24,540
[KAT]
Hey! Is anyone around?

162
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:27,960
This place is even
more run-down than I thought.

163
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:28,960
Kat's here!

164
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,920
[ELLIOTT] Sure kept us
in suspense, didn't you?

165
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,670
And then you show up
at the break of dawn!

166
00:08:33,750 --> 00:08:36,380
So am I too early, or too late?
Make up your mind.

167
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:37,710
[panting]

168
00:08:37,790 --> 00:08:40,250
- [ANNE] Kat!
- Oh. Hey, pipsqueak.

169
00:08:40,330 --> 00:08:42,130
Thank you so much
for coming to help us!

170
00:08:42,210 --> 00:08:44,750
But wait.
We hadn't sent word to you yet.

171
00:08:44,830 --> 00:08:47,080
We won the favor from Hugh,
like we had planned

172
00:08:47,170 --> 00:08:49,460
but I don't know
how you could've known that.

173
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:51,330
There's only one way, right?

174
00:08:51,420 --> 00:08:53,580
That dimwit came and told
me himself.

175
00:08:53,670 --> 00:08:56,170
Not sure why he found it
so amusing.

176
00:08:56,250 --> 00:08:58,500
Anyway, he also told me
to give you this.

177
00:08:58,580 --> 00:08:59,960
A present?

178
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:02,420
Huh! Why,
it must be a love letter!

179
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:03,880
I wonder who it could be from?

180
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,670
Enough! If you want my help,

181
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:07,630
then show me
to the workroom already!

182
00:09:07,710 --> 00:09:09,380
Right. Fair point.

183
00:09:09,460 --> 00:09:11,250
First, I'll introduce you
to the artisans

184
00:09:11,330 --> 00:09:12,330
you'll be working with.

185
00:09:12,420 --> 00:09:14,630
I'll go deliver
the good news to Mister Glen.

186
00:09:14,710 --> 00:09:16,580
Hmm! Splendid. Thanks.

187
00:09:18,290 --> 00:09:21,380
[GLEN] Alph Hingley is here
and he's going to help us?

188
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:22,540
[ANNE]
Yes, sir.

189
00:09:22,630 --> 00:09:25,210
Right now, Mister Collins is
introducing him to everyone.

190
00:09:25,290 --> 00:09:27,580
[sighs] I'm glad.

191
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,630
We still have
poor Orland's injury

192
00:09:30,710 --> 00:09:31,880
to worry about, though.

193
00:09:33,290 --> 00:09:34,210
Mister Glen.

194
00:09:35,130 --> 00:09:37,250
Have you seen Miss Bridget
since that happened?

195
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:39,960
[GLEN]
I have not.

196
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:41,080
Hmm!

197
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:46,130
[GLEN] Anne.
I know what you want to say.

198
00:09:46,210 --> 00:09:47,130
Huh?

199
00:09:47,210 --> 00:09:50,830
But right now, I can't stand
to see her face. I'm angry.

200
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:54,040
Her selfishness
has harmed us all.

201
00:09:54,130 --> 00:09:55,330
And in the case of Orland,

202
00:09:55,420 --> 00:09:57,460
it might have harmed him
irreparably.

203
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,130
[sighs]

204
00:10:03,630 --> 00:10:05,880
You treat other people too well.

205
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:08,250
Right now, you should worry
about your own problems.

206
00:10:09,460 --> 00:10:10,830
Hmm-mmm!

207
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:12,750
[ELLIOTT]
Anne!

208
00:10:12,830 --> 00:10:13,830
Coming!

209
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:17,210
Uh! What is it?

210
00:10:17,290 --> 00:10:20,000
Sorry, but we need to take
a quick little trip.

211
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:22,670
I've been summoned.
The church wants to talk.

212
00:10:24,630 --> 00:10:26,130
[HEAD PRIEST]
Thank you for coming.

213
00:10:26,790 --> 00:10:28,880
I spoke
to the Silver Sugar Viscount.

214
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:32,170
He informed me that your work
hasn't been progressing well.

215
00:10:32,250 --> 00:10:34,540
You haven't completed
a single piece,

216
00:10:34,630 --> 00:10:36,630
and you're re-grinding
silver sugar

217
00:10:36,710 --> 00:10:39,580
which hardened after
it was exposed to moisture.

218
00:10:39,670 --> 00:10:41,750
He also said that one
of your artisans

219
00:10:41,830 --> 00:10:42,880
has been injured.

220
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:44,420
Is that an accurate assessment?

221
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:46,960
Yes, sir, that's correct.

222
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:49,130
A month and a half.

223
00:10:49,210 --> 00:10:52,170
Unfortunately,
given the current situation,

224
00:10:52,250 --> 00:10:55,670
your workshop won't be able
to complete the pieces in time.

225
00:10:55,750 --> 00:10:57,460
There's simply
no other conclusion.

226
00:10:58,420 --> 00:11:00,540
We need to think quickly.

227
00:11:00,630 --> 00:11:03,130
Perhaps, the Mercury Workshop
could step in

228
00:11:03,210 --> 00:11:04,670
and finish it on your behalf?

229
00:11:04,750 --> 00:11:06,880
Huh! But that would mean...

230
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,210
[HEAD PRIEST]
You would step down

231
00:11:08,290 --> 00:11:10,960
and their artisans would
create your pieces for you.

232
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:12,290
[gasps]

233
00:11:14,290 --> 00:11:16,670
[ANNE] I couldn't possibly hand
the project over!

234
00:11:16,750 --> 00:11:18,420
This is our creation!

235
00:11:19,250 --> 00:11:21,580
[HEAD PRIEST] Please don't see
this as a punishment.

236
00:11:21,670 --> 00:11:23,040
You've simply been the victim

237
00:11:23,130 --> 00:11:25,710
of circumstances
beyond your control.

238
00:11:25,790 --> 00:11:26,710
It's a shame,

239
00:11:26,790 --> 00:11:28,540
which is why
we will still pay you

240
00:11:28,630 --> 00:11:31,960
all the reward of 10,000 cress.
How does that sound?

241
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:33,880
[sighs]

242
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:35,880
Aha! Sounds lovely!

243
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:37,210
Mister Collins!

244
00:11:37,290 --> 00:11:38,500
It's very generous!

245
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:39,920
We don't have to suffer any more

246
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,750
and we still get
the nice reward, don't we?

247
00:11:41,830 --> 00:11:43,040
I refuse!

248
00:11:43,130 --> 00:11:45,670
We've done this as a team.
It was our idea!

249
00:11:45,750 --> 00:11:48,420
I can't bear the thought
of someone else making it!

250
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:50,210
If we sell off our work now,

251
00:11:50,290 --> 00:11:52,920
we'll be selling our pride
as artisans along with it!

252
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:56,460
Then there would've been
no point in making it this far!

253
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:58,040
You think so?

254
00:11:58,130 --> 00:12:00,500
It's not just
what I think, it's a fact!

255
00:12:00,580 --> 00:12:01,460
That's fair enough!

256
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:02,420
Huh?

257
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:03,830
[ELLIOTT]
As you've just heard,

258
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:06,250
our Head of Artisans
does not accept your deal,

259
00:12:06,330 --> 00:12:08,420
and the rest of the workshop
stands beside her.

260
00:12:09,580 --> 00:12:12,130
So, we will decline
your generous offer.

261
00:12:12,210 --> 00:12:13,880
We will complete
the sugar confections

262
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:16,170
for the Holy
Beginnings Festival.

263
00:12:16,250 --> 00:12:17,580
You're certain?

264
00:12:17,670 --> 00:12:19,000
[ELLIOTT]
There's no need to worry.

265
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:20,670
We will meet the deadline.

266
00:12:20,750 --> 00:12:21,880
[sighs]

267
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:24,380
If your stubbornness
causes you to fail the job,

268
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:26,580
we will not be able
to pay you the reward.

269
00:12:26,670 --> 00:12:30,130
Then, the Paige Workshop's
reputation will hit rock bottom.

270
00:12:30,210 --> 00:12:31,580
We are aware of the risk.

271
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:34,710
Hmm!

272
00:12:36,670 --> 00:12:39,130
[ELLIOTT] Well, I made all
those confident declarations,

273
00:12:39,210 --> 00:12:40,960
but it's only natural
for the church

274
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:42,830
to be worried about this.

275
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:44,580
I'm grateful that we have Kat
to help us,

276
00:12:44,670 --> 00:12:46,330
but considering that Orland
is stuck in bed,

277
00:12:46,420 --> 00:12:47,750
- we haven't gained anyone.
- [ANNE] It's him.

278
00:12:47,830 --> 00:12:49,710
- We are just breaking even.
- One moment!

279
00:12:49,790 --> 00:12:51,080
Could you please stop the cart!?

280
00:12:51,170 --> 00:12:52,330
Well, all right?

281
00:12:52,420 --> 00:12:54,330
Please! You'll catch a cold!

282
00:12:54,420 --> 00:12:57,500
Don't doze off in an alley!
Get up, I'm begging you!

283
00:12:57,580 --> 00:12:59,210
We can't go on like this!

284
00:12:59,290 --> 00:13:00,540
[ANNE]
Cathy!

285
00:13:00,630 --> 00:13:02,380
Huh! It's you!

286
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:04,670
[ANNE]
Jonas.

287
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:17,000
- [knocks]
- Huh!

288
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:20,330
- [creaks]
- Miss! Good to see you!

289
00:13:20,420 --> 00:13:21,540
I just...

290
00:13:23,130 --> 00:13:25,250
Is Orland doing any better?

291
00:13:25,330 --> 00:13:26,290
Mister Orland!

292
00:13:26,380 --> 00:13:28,080
- Miss Bridget is here for you!
- Hold on. I'm not...

293
00:13:28,170 --> 00:13:30,290
One moment.
I'll go bring you some tea.

294
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:32,170
Huh!

295
00:13:33,830 --> 00:13:37,290
♪

296
00:13:38,130 --> 00:13:39,130
What's wrong?

297
00:13:40,250 --> 00:13:41,380
Are you all right?

298
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:44,920
My eye? I'll be fine.

299
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,790
No need to worry.

300
00:13:46,880 --> 00:13:49,670
I still have my right one.
I'm not blind.

301
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:52,290
Luckily, my fingers
are intact, too.

302
00:13:52,380 --> 00:13:53,580
And Kat came to help.

303
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:56,630
- More importantly.
- Huh!

304
00:13:57,790 --> 00:14:00,290
He didn't hurt you
and that's enough.

305
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:03,460
[sobs]

306
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:09,710
It's my fault.
I'm so sorry. Forgive me.

307
00:14:11,380 --> 00:14:12,210
This only happened

308
00:14:12,290 --> 00:14:14,210
because I brought
that fairy here.

309
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:17,830
[sobs]

310
00:14:19,790 --> 00:14:23,040
It's not much
but could I take care of you?

311
00:14:24,630 --> 00:14:27,210
I won't force you!
I'll leave if you like.

312
00:14:28,710 --> 00:14:31,580
I'm not the person
I used to be, after all.

313
00:14:31,670 --> 00:14:33,790
I'm arrogant and selfish.

314
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:37,710
I don't expect anyone
to like me or even tolerate me.

315
00:14:37,790 --> 00:14:40,460
♪

316
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:42,290
Please stay.

317
00:14:42,380 --> 00:14:43,380
You mean it?

318
00:14:43,460 --> 00:14:46,250
♪

319
00:14:53,500 --> 00:14:55,830
[ANNE]
Jonas? Jonas, are you sleeping?

320
00:14:56,750 --> 00:14:58,380
Jonas, I'm talking to you!

321
00:14:59,080 --> 00:15:00,830
[groans]

322
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:04,420
Anne. Anne?
Wha-What do you want?

323
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:06,170
Why are you even here
in the first place?

324
00:15:06,250 --> 00:15:07,750
[ANNE]
Stop! Come back!

325
00:15:07,830 --> 00:15:09,920
You remember what happened
at the exhibition, right?

326
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,830
I'm trying to forget, thank you!

327
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:13,500
Just listen, would you?

328
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:15,790
The situation isn't
what you think it is!

329
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:17,330
The things Sammy
did were brought to light

330
00:15:17,420 --> 00:15:18,630
at the exhibition.

331
00:15:18,710 --> 00:15:21,210
Jonas, they proved
your innocence!

332
00:15:21,290 --> 00:15:22,170
Ah!

333
00:15:23,210 --> 00:15:24,130
Really?

334
00:15:24,210 --> 00:15:27,330
Mister Radcliffe said
he wanted to apologize to you.

335
00:15:27,420 --> 00:15:28,880
I heard that he wants
you to come back

336
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:30,130
to the workshop, as well!

337
00:15:30,210 --> 00:15:32,290
Master Jonas,
this is wonderful news!

338
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:34,330
We should get ready to go
as soon as we can!

339
00:15:36,580 --> 00:15:38,000
[ANNE]
Jonas?

340
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,750
I won't go back there.

341
00:15:39,830 --> 00:15:42,880
I'm confused.
It was a misunderstanding!

342
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:43,790
There's no reason

343
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:45,630
why anyone there would
hold this against you.

344
00:15:45,710 --> 00:15:46,670
So, what's wrong?

345
00:15:46,750 --> 00:15:48,420
♪

346
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:51,210
If I go to their workshop,
Kieth will still be there.

347
00:15:51,290 --> 00:15:52,710
I'll just be compared to him

348
00:15:52,790 --> 00:15:54,420
and feel wretched
all over again.

349
00:15:55,250 --> 00:15:56,750
Huh! No, wait!

350
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,880
You've said enough, all right!?

351
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:00,960
[ANNE]
Jonas.

352
00:16:01,670 --> 00:16:04,210
Will you come
to the Paige Workshop instead?

353
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:06,540
[JONAS]
Paige's Workshop?

354
00:16:06,630 --> 00:16:09,880
Right now, I'm working
on an urgent project with them.

355
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:10,790
We're having trouble

356
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:12,830
because we don't have
enough artisans.

357
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:13,830
With your skills,

358
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:15,500
you would be a valuable asset.

359
00:16:16,250 --> 00:16:17,080
What do you think?

360
00:16:17,170 --> 00:16:18,130
I can't believe you,

361
00:16:18,210 --> 00:16:20,790
you're always doing
such absurd things.

362
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:23,920
I'm sick of making confections
and that's the end of it!

363
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,630
If I never touch
silver sugar again

364
00:16:25,710 --> 00:16:26,830
then I'll be happy!

365
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:27,920
Huh!

366
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,540
I have other plans now.

367
00:16:29,630 --> 00:16:31,630
Things that I would
much rather do.

368
00:16:32,630 --> 00:16:35,960
I can't make it any clearer
than that! Now, goodbye!

369
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:38,920
What is it you want to do?
Drink until you're sick?

370
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:41,670
Pass out in a cold, dirty alley

371
00:16:41,750 --> 00:16:43,290
and make Cathy worry about you?

372
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:46,460
Do nothing
and keep making up excuses?

373
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:47,880
[sighs]

374
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:48,830
[JONAS]
Go away.

375
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:52,630
Not yet. Not 'til you can at
least be honest with me, Jonas!

376
00:16:52,710 --> 00:16:56,130
Enough! Someone like
you could never understand me!

377
00:16:56,210 --> 00:16:57,170
Huh!

378
00:16:57,880 --> 00:17:00,830
What do you mean,
"someone like me?" Why?

379
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:04,670
You can still make confections,
like before.

380
00:17:04,750 --> 00:17:06,080
Uh!

381
00:17:06,170 --> 00:17:09,420
I knew it. You haven't given up.

382
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:11,790
In your heart,
you still want to do it.

383
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:13,830
[JONAS]
No! I told you! I...

384
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:19,460
After all that's happened,
how could, I how could I?

385
00:17:19,540 --> 00:17:21,500
[sobs]

386
00:17:22,540 --> 00:17:24,040
But I want to.

387
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:27,290
Master Jonas.

388
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:29,420
[sobs]

389
00:17:30,210 --> 00:17:33,130
[CHALLE] It would seem
we've recruited a new artisan.

390
00:17:33,210 --> 00:17:35,290
Seems like
he's got self-esteem issues

391
00:17:35,380 --> 00:17:37,210
but he might be reliable
in a pinch.

392
00:17:37,290 --> 00:17:38,330
Let's hope.

393
00:17:40,330 --> 00:17:41,540
[KAT]
What did you drag in?

394
00:17:41,630 --> 00:17:44,880
Uh...
Actually, I think I'll leave.

395
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:47,420
[ANNE]
Wait! This is Jonas Anders!

396
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:49,790
He's an artisan from the
Radcliffe Workshop school!

397
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:51,500
He used to be my rival!

398
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:54,460
"Rival?" Then,
he must be pretty skilled, huh?

399
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:55,960
All right! We'll see!

400
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:58,920
- We could sure use your help!
- Jonas, come here.

401
00:18:02,250 --> 00:18:03,500
[sighs]

402
00:18:04,330 --> 00:18:05,920
[KAT]
Nice craftsmanship, right?

403
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:07,880
I was impressed, as well.

404
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:11,210
Alas, these take an
absurd amount of time to make.

405
00:18:11,290 --> 00:18:13,330
And they're also very delicate.

406
00:18:13,420 --> 00:18:15,080
If you handle them wrong,
they'll collapse.

407
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:17,630
I want to make sure
that you understand

408
00:18:17,710 --> 00:18:19,580
what's being asked of you.

409
00:18:19,670 --> 00:18:21,540
- Huh!
- Hmm!

410
00:18:22,750 --> 00:18:23,750
Hmm!

411
00:18:26,330 --> 00:18:27,830
[gasps]

412
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:28,960
What's wrong?

413
00:18:29,710 --> 00:18:31,830
[whooshes]

414
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:33,790
[footsteps]

415
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:35,630
[panting]

416
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:37,830
I messed up.

417
00:18:37,920 --> 00:18:38,830
[CHALLE]
Lafalle's back.

418
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:40,830
What happened?

419
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:42,290
Why has he done this to you?

420
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:44,790
[groans]

421
00:18:46,580 --> 00:18:48,710
[chuckles]

422
00:18:48,790 --> 00:18:52,380
[CHALLE] Elliott, you must have
a message from him. Tell us.

423
00:18:53,170 --> 00:18:54,500
[ELLIOTT]
Can't do that.

424
00:18:54,580 --> 00:18:56,710
[CHALLE]
Don't worry! Say it!

425
00:18:57,580 --> 00:18:58,960
Hand over Anne,

426
00:18:59,040 --> 00:19:02,170
he'll release me in exchange,
he said. I'm sorry.

427
00:19:02,250 --> 00:19:03,960
How cruel!

428
00:19:04,040 --> 00:19:05,960
[whooshes]

429
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,540
[clangs]

430
00:19:09,500 --> 00:19:11,250
Challe, please don't!

431
00:19:11,330 --> 00:19:12,710
[gasps]

432
00:19:12,790 --> 00:19:13,880
Anne!

433
00:19:15,670 --> 00:19:16,830
It's fine.

434
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:19,790
♪

435
00:19:19,880 --> 00:19:22,580
[grunts]

436
00:19:29,290 --> 00:19:30,670
- [JONAS] Someone help!
- [KAT] Be careful! - Elliott!

437
00:19:30,750 --> 00:19:34,170
It's your turn, Challe.
Come here. Slowly.

438
00:19:34,250 --> 00:19:38,130
♪

439
00:19:38,210 --> 00:19:42,290
[footsteps]

440
00:19:48,830 --> 00:19:50,790
- Stop it!
- You bastard!

441
00:19:50,880 --> 00:19:52,380
[LAFALLE]
Oh, quiet.

442
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:53,500
If you misbehave,

443
00:19:53,580 --> 00:19:55,460
then her pretty, little head
will come off.

444
00:19:56,540 --> 00:19:58,630
Keep walking,
with your hands in sight.

445
00:19:59,420 --> 00:20:01,330
I wouldn't try anything rash,

446
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:04,460
or I may, in my distress,
cut off one of Anne's legs.

447
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:08,670
I will have your wing now.

448
00:20:08,750 --> 00:20:10,960
♪

449
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:12,580
[ALL gasp]

450
00:20:13,630 --> 00:20:14,670
[gasps]

451
00:20:16,170 --> 00:20:17,750
[LAFALLE]
Take it from him, Anne.

452
00:20:17,830 --> 00:20:21,830
♪

453
00:20:26,250 --> 00:20:28,080
Splendid.

454
00:20:28,170 --> 00:20:29,330
[groans]

455
00:20:30,130 --> 00:20:31,040
[ANNE]
No, Challe!

456
00:20:31,130 --> 00:20:32,500
That settles it!

457
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:34,710
Seems this is, indeed,
your wing.

458
00:20:34,790 --> 00:20:36,500
Now, get on that horse there.

459
00:20:37,250 --> 00:20:39,420
I readied it just for you,
Challe.

460
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:42,080
I thought you would appreciate
its beautiful black coat.

461
00:20:42,170 --> 00:20:43,460
[grunts]

462
00:20:43,540 --> 00:20:44,580
[purring]

463
00:20:44,670 --> 00:20:45,710
[gasps]

464
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:50,710
♪

465
00:20:50,790 --> 00:20:52,210
[neighs]

466
00:20:53,330 --> 00:20:57,710
♪

